{%- comment -%}
  Dynamic Pricing block. Renders a skeleton the storefront JS (assets/dynamic-pricing.js)
  fills in from GET/POST /apps/imprintid-pricing/pricing — see docs/storefront-pricing-ui.md.
  No pricing value is written here or in that JS; every dollar amount comes from the
  pricing API response at request time.

  SKU resolution: the merchant's "Override SKU" setting takes precedence when set
  (useful for previewing the block before a product's real SKU is assigned); otherwise
  this uses the current product's first available variant's SKU, since SKUs in Shopify
  belong to variants, not products. If neither resolves to a non-empty value, the block
  renders its "unavailable" state and never calls the pricing API.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign pricing_product = block.settings.product | default: product -%}
{%- assign resolved_sku = block.settings.sku_override | default: pricing_product.selected_or_first_available_variant.sku -%}

{%- comment -%}
  TASK 2B — variant synchronization metadata. Re-audited for Task 2B.1, requirement 3
  ("verify safe Liquid serialization") — confirmed correct as-is; nothing below changed
  as a result, since re-escaping an already-correct value would double-encode it. The
  reasoning, laid out explicitly here because that's what was asked for:

  `data-variant-map` is PUBLIC storefront metadata (every variant's numeric id, SKU, and
  availability — nothing a customer can't already see by opening the variant picker) —
  it is a lookup table the storefront JS cross-checks a *claimed* variant id against
  before trusting it, never a source of pricing itself. Real pricing is always
  recomputed and signed server-side (see app/lib/pricing-api/storefront-handler.ts);
  this map only ever answers "does this numeric id correspond to a real variant of THIS
  product, and if so what's its SKU/availability" — see dynamic-pricing.js's
  `resolveVariantFromMap`.

  TWO SEPARATE ENCODING LAYERS, each doing a different job:
    1. `variant.sku | json` — every merchant-controlled value (only the SKU; `available`
       is a real boolean, not free text) is JSON-string-escaped by Liquid's `json`
       filter before being placed inside the captured JSON text. This is what makes a
       SKU containing a quote, backslash, ampersand, angle bracket, or Unicode character
       represent safely *as JSON* — `json` produces a valid JSON string token no matter
       what the SKU contains.
    2. `variant_map_json | escape` — the ENTIRE captured JSON string (including its own
       structural `"` characters from step 1, not just merchant content) is then
       HTML-attribute-escaped as one unit, because it's being embedded inside a
       double-quoted HTML attribute (`data-variant-map="..."` below), not inside a
       `<script>` block. This is what stops the JSON's own literal `"` characters from
       prematurely closing the HTML attribute. A browser's HTML parser automatically
       reverses exactly this escaping when it reads the attribute value back out (that's
       ordinary HTML entity decoding, not something the JS needs to do) — so
       `element.dataset.variantMap` in dynamic-pricing.js receives the original,
       unescaped JSON text, ready for `JSON.parse` (via `parseVariantMap`). Because the
       value lives in an HTML ATTRIBUTE, not `<script>` element content, it is not
       subject to the `</script>`-closing-tag-injection class of issue at all — that
       risk only applies to text placed inside a script element's body (which is a
       reason NOT to move this to a nested `<script type="application/json">`; the
       current attribute-based approach is already immune to it, not merely mitigated).

  `variant.id` is used ONLY as this JSON object's key (`"{{ variant.id }}":`) — JSON
  object keys are syntactically always strings (the surrounding literal `"` characters
  make it one), so this is never emitted as a bare JSON number. `variant.id` itself is a
  Shopify-platform-guaranteed positive integer, never merchant-editable free text, so
  interpolating it raw (rather than through `json`, which would turn an integer into an
  UNQUOTED JSON number and break the key syntax) is deliberate and safe.

  Parsing failure fails closed: `parseVariantMap` (dynamic-pricing-utils.js) returns `{}`
  for anything that isn't valid, well-shaped JSON — never throws, never partially trusts
  a malformed map.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture variant_map_json -%}
{
{%- for variant in pricing_product.variants -%}
"{{ variant.id }}":{"sku":{{ variant.sku | json }},"available":{{ variant.available | json }}}{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
{%- endfor -%}
}
{%- endcapture -%}

<div
  class="imprintid-pricing"
  data-imprintid-pricing
  data-sku="{{ resolved_sku | escape }}"
  data-variant-id="{{ pricing_product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}"
  data-variant-sku="{{ pricing_product.selected_or_first_available_variant.sku | escape }}"
  data-variant-available="{{ pricing_product.selected_or_first_available_variant.available }}"
  data-product-id="{{ pricing_product.id }}"
  data-product-gid="gid://shopify/Product/{{ pricing_product.id }}"
  data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
  data-variant-map="{{ variant_map_json | escape }}"
  data-proxy-path="/apps/imprintid-pricing/pricing"
  data-show-breakdown="{{ block.settings.show_breakdown_by_default }}"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <h3 class="imprintid-pricing__heading">{{ 'dynamic_pricing.heading' | t }}</h3>

  <p class="imprintid-pricing__unavailable" data-imprintid-pricing-unavailable hidden>
    {{ 'dynamic_pricing.unsupported_product' | t }}
  </p>

  <p class="imprintid-pricing__loading" data-imprintid-pricing-loading hidden aria-live="polite">
    {{ 'dynamic_pricing.loading_options' | t }}
  </p>

  <div class="imprintid-pricing__panel" data-imprintid-pricing-panel hidden>
    <form data-imprintid-pricing-form novalidate>
      <div class="imprintid-pricing__field">
        <label for="imprintid-pricing-quantity-{{ block.id }}">{{ 'dynamic_pricing.quantity_label' | t }}</label>
        <input
          type="number"
          id="imprintid-pricing-quantity-{{ block.id }}"
          name="quantity"
          data-imprintid-pricing-quantity
          min="1"
          step="1"
          inputmode="numeric"
          aria-describedby="imprintid-pricing-quantity-error-{{ block.id }}"
        >
        <p id="imprintid-pricing-quantity-error-{{ block.id }}" class="imprintid-pricing__field-error" data-imprintid-pricing-quantity-error hidden role="alert"></p>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} Only shown when the catalog actually returns configured product
         colors (see STEP 3, Phase 2.7) — LNY01 has none today, so this stays hidden for
         it; the control exists generically for any future product that does. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="imprintid-pricing__field" data-imprintid-pricing-color-wrap hidden>
        <label for="imprintid-pricing-color-{{ block.id }}">{{ 'dynamic_pricing.color_label' | t }}</label>
        <select id="imprintid-pricing-color-{{ block.id }}" data-imprintid-pricing-color></select>
      </div>

      <fieldset class="imprintid-pricing__field" data-imprintid-pricing-decoration-fieldset>
        <legend>{{ 'dynamic_pricing.decoration_legend' | t }}</legend>

        <div class="imprintid-pricing__field">
          <label for="imprintid-pricing-colors-{{ block.id }}">{{ 'dynamic_pricing.colors_label' | t }}</label>
          <select id="imprintid-pricing-colors-{{ block.id }}" data-imprintid-pricing-colors>
            <option value="1">{{ 'dynamic_pricing.colors_one' | t }}</option>
            <option value="2">{{ 'dynamic_pricing.colors_two' | t }}</option>
          </select>
        </div>

        <div class="imprintid-pricing__field">
          <label for="imprintid-pricing-locations-{{ block.id }}">{{ 'dynamic_pricing.locations_label' | t }}</label>
          <select id="imprintid-pricing-locations-{{ block.id }}" data-imprintid-pricing-locations>
            <option value="1">{{ 'dynamic_pricing.locations_one' | t }}</option>
            <option value="2">{{ 'dynamic_pricing.locations_two' | t }}</option>
          </select>
        </div>

        <div class="imprintid-pricing__field imprintid-pricing__field--checkbox">
          <input type="checkbox" id="imprintid-pricing-reverse-{{ block.id }}" data-imprintid-pricing-reverse-side>
          <label for="imprintid-pricing-reverse-{{ block.id }}">{{ 'dynamic_pricing.reverse_side_label' | t }}</label>
        </div>

        <div class="imprintid-pricing__field imprintid-pricing__field--checkbox" data-imprintid-pricing-reverse-artwork-wrap hidden>
          <input type="checkbox" id="imprintid-pricing-reverse-artwork-{{ block.id }}" data-imprintid-pricing-reverse-artwork>
          <label for="imprintid-pricing-reverse-artwork-{{ block.id }}">{{ 'dynamic_pricing.different_reverse_artwork_label' | t }}</label>
        </div>

        <div class="imprintid-pricing__field imprintid-pricing__field--checkbox">
          <input type="checkbox" id="imprintid-pricing-repeat-{{ block.id }}" data-imprintid-pricing-repeat-order>
          <label for="imprintid-pricing-repeat-{{ block.id }}">{{ 'dynamic_pricing.repeat_order_label' | t }}</label>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <div class="imprintid-pricing__options" data-imprintid-pricing-options>
        {%- comment -%} One <select> per OptionGroup is inserted here by JS, built from the real catalog response — never hardcoded. {%- endcomment -%}
      </div>

      <div class="imprintid-pricing__field">
        <label for="imprintid-pricing-production-{{ block.id }}">{{ 'dynamic_pricing.production_label' | t }}</label>
        <select id="imprintid-pricing-production-{{ block.id }}" data-imprintid-pricing-production></select>
        <p class="imprintid-pricing__hint" data-imprintid-pricing-production-hint></p>
      </div>
    </form>

    <div class="imprintid-pricing__result" data-imprintid-pricing-result aria-live="polite">
      <div class="imprintid-pricing__unit-prices">
        <div>
          <span class="imprintid-pricing__unit-label">{{ 'dynamic_pricing.list_price_label' | t }}</span>
          <span data-imprintid-pricing-list-unit>—</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="imprintid-pricing__unit-label">{{ 'dynamic_pricing.your_price_label' | t }}</span>
          <span data-imprintid-pricing-net-unit>—</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="imprintid-pricing__total">
        <span class="imprintid-pricing__total-label">{{ 'dynamic_pricing.total_label' | t }}</span>
        <span data-imprintid-pricing-total>—</span>
      </div>

      <p class="imprintid-pricing__tier-note" data-imprintid-pricing-tier-note></p>

      <table class="imprintid-pricing__tier-table" data-imprintid-pricing-tier-table hidden>
        <caption>{{ 'dynamic_pricing.quantity_breaks_caption' | t }}</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">{{ 'dynamic_pricing.quantity_breaks_qty_header' | t }}</th>
            <th scope="col">{{ 'dynamic_pricing.list_price_label' | t }}</th>
            <th scope="col">{{ 'dynamic_pricing.your_price_label' | t }}</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody data-imprintid-pricing-tier-table-body></tbody>
      </table>

      <details class="imprintid-pricing__breakdown" data-imprintid-pricing-breakdown>
        <summary>{{ 'dynamic_pricing.breakdown_summary' | t }}</summary>
        <dl data-imprintid-pricing-breakdown-list></dl>
      </details>
    </div>

    <p class="imprintid-pricing__error" data-imprintid-pricing-error hidden role="alert"></p>

    {%- comment -%} Add to Cart is only ever enabled once a genuine, server-signed
       cartPricing payload has come back for the current configuration (see
       dynamic-pricing.js#renderResult) — the button itself never carries or computes a
       price; it only adds the real Shopify variant to cart with that signed payload
       attached as line properties, for imprintid-cart-pricing (the Cart Transform
       Function) to verify and enforce. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="imprintid-pricing__actions">
      <button
        type="button"
        class="imprintid-pricing__add-to-cart"
        data-imprintid-pricing-add-to-cart
        disabled
      >
        {{ 'dynamic_pricing.add_to_cart' | t }}
      </button>
      <p class="imprintid-pricing__add-to-cart-status" data-imprintid-pricing-add-to-cart-status aria-live="polite"></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{{ 'dynamic-pricing.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
